From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: b43: HT-PHY: fill in the duration of MCS frames

mac80211 leaves the Duration field of frames sent at an MCS rate to the
hardware (ieee80211_duration() returns 0 for them), and the b43 ucode sends
it as it is: a capture showed Duration 0 in every one of 126833 A-MPDU
subframes. Other stations then set no NAV for the ACK or block ack that
follows, and only physical carrier sense protects the answer.

Set SIFS plus the ACK, or the compressed block ack (32 bytes) of an A-MPDU,
at the response rate, as brcms_c_compute_frame_dur() does; the response
rate is the one the RTS/CTS patch uses for MCS frames, the fastest basic
OFDM rate up to 24 Mbit/s (6 Mbit/s when the BSS has none). Group addressed
and no-ack frames keep 0.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
index 217f0b0..13c2a30 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
@@ -631,6 +631,23 @@ int b43_generate_txhdr(struct b43_wldev *dev,
 		sgi = rates[0].flags & IEEE80211_TX_RC_SHORT_GI;
 		sgi_fb = rfb->flags & IEEE80211_TX_RC_SHORT_GI;
 
+		/* mac80211 leaves the duration of MCS frames to the hardware,
+		 * which sends 0: other stations then set no NAV for the
+		 * answer. Cover SIFS and the ACK, or the block ack of an
+		 * A-MPDU, at the response rate (brcms_c_compute_frame_dur) */
+		if (!wlhdr->duration_id && !is_multicast_ether_addr(wlhdr->addr1) &&
+		    !(info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_ACK)) {
+			struct ieee80211_rate *r = b43_ht_rts_rate(dev, info);
+			unsigned int mbps = r ? r->bitrate / 10 : 6;
+			unsigned int bytes =
+				info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_AMPDU ? 32 : 14;
+
+			((struct ieee80211_hdr *)skb_frag->data)->duration_id =
+				cpu_to_le16(B43_SIFS_US + 20 + 6 +
+					    DIV_ROUND_UP(16 + 8 * bytes + 6,
+							 mbps * 4) * 4);
+		}
+
 		switch (dev->fw.hdr_format) {
 		case B43_FW_HDR_598:
 			plcp = txhdr->format_598.plcp.raw;
